  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Acquisition of the Mask
    
    After Augur ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ the Resolute died in the Abyss Collapse Tide, ☽'visois' Mask — the shadow-steel artifact that selects its own wielders — entered a prolonged evaluation cycle at Thrall☽ Vavmastius. The process lasted multiple seasons and was complicated by the Profun∴lapsum, a geothermal catastrophe that killed dozens of candidates and forced the colony into debt. Lucatransiius, a young Nightshelf fire-keeper serving on rescue teams, first encountered the mask three days after the Collapse, sitting on an ice shelf carved by no recognized tool. The surviving Mask-perspective assessment designates Lucatransiius as Candidate 23, with a grief profile of 7.1 — precisely within the artifact's acceptable range for someone capable of carrying unbearable weight without breaking. Lucatransiius reported feeling every previous wielder watching through the crack along the mask's left cheekbone. The artifact projected a thirty-year tenure.
    
    ## Service Under the Mask
    
    With the mask, Lucatransiius served as enforcer of Pactum∴ne, the trade charter governing fire-core shipments through the Drowned Ledge — walking routes, ensuring compliance. During the Faction Wars, Lucatransiius operated as the shadow of Veil-render Seciae~, the Nightshelf hero who led ☽'scar Ramtatus~ through its founding violence: second through every breach, responsible for ensuring Seciae~ walked out alive. The chronicles do not call this heroism. Between shifts, Lucatransiius brought Seciae~ fire-tea in chipped volcanic glass, sharing from the same cup — a gesture both understood and neither named.
    
    During ☽'scar Ramtatus~'s expansion, Lucatransiius carried the mask through the mapping of twelve new shafts. In shaft eight, miners reported an anomalous cold consuming heat from veins showing no sign of depletion. Lucatransiius and Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss assessed the evidence and declared it vein depletion — a determination Lucatransiius signed with their own flipper-print in ash, because the colony needed those yields and the Flipper Accord was non-negotiable. Privately, Lucatransiius told Seciae~ the unmapped deep ice had been left uncharted for reasons. Later accounts from Seciae~'s own perspective confirm the wrongness persisted and worsened, suggesting the official assessment was, at minimum, premature.
    
    When the Profun∴lapsum flooded the deep tunnels with superheated steam, Lucatransiius pulled two fire-tenders from a collapsing shaft and carried a third on their back through conditions that left their armor blackened.
    
    ## Loss of the Mask
    
    At sanctification rites at Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius during the Orca Incursion, Lucatransiius set the mask on a shelf of worked ice. In their absence, the weapon chose ☽'Netemia Glow-bringer as its next bearer. Lucatransiius's flippers bore permanent scarring where the mask's edges had written themselves into their flesh. They kept their grip-hand wrapped in ash-gray cloth for the remainder of their life.
    
    Lucatransiius continued as Pactum∴ne enforcer, authority derived from the charter rather than the artifact.
    
    ## Final Stand and Death
    
    During the Frozen Peace, Lucatransiius stood alone against orca raiders on the ice and did not leave. Their spear carved a wound into the flank of Gnarkzund Zaith, an orca raider whose forces would later besiege ☽'slew Ravium~ and die at Aurora Stack — a wound Nightshelf sources claim never fully closed, reopening in combat generations later. The same engagement scarred the left flank of Thung Thrakrek, Gnarkzund Zaith's bond-mate.
    
    Whether wounds from a single penguin's last stand materially affected an orca commander's subsequent campaigns is not attested in any source I have reviewed. But the Nightshelf needed the story to mean something, and stories about what the dead accomplished have a way of growing to fill the silence they left.
    
    ## Commemoration
    
    The site of the stand is preserved under Umbra∴go, a Frozen Peace memorial rule forbidding the ice from being worked, carved, or melted — a protection that has since accumulated the weight of every Nightshelf catastrophe from the Silent War to the Extinction of the Deep-Singers. The memorial at Vestigium∴moria lists Lucatransiius among those who saved the colony. Nightshelf children are told the name in the dark, in the way one speaks of debts that cannot be repaid.
