  annotation "note_1771577838713_0", anchor: "grief profile of 7.1 — precisely within the artifact's acceptable range", text: "The Mask-perspective assessment is a document that assigns numerical grief scores to bereaved penguins and then ranks them by load-bearing capacity. Twenty-two candidates were evaluated before Lucatransiius. The Nightshelf filed this under 'liturgical records.' I have filed it under 'things that explain everything about Nightshelf institutional culture in a single page.'", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771577838713_1", anchor: "sitting on an ice shelf carved by no recognized tool", text: "Unrecognized is not unrecognizable. The cut-marks match impressions I have catalogued from strata predating any penguin civilization — deep enough that I stopped mentioning them in reports because no one was reading the reports. The Mask found its way to a surface prepared for it by something that has been waiting longer than we have been counting.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771577838713_2", anchor: "The chronicles do not call this heroism", text: "They do, however, record the tea. The chipped volcanic glass. The shared cup. Someone thought this mattered enough to freeze into the operational record of a wartime command structure. The chronicles are correct that it is not heroism. It is breakfast. I find I have no professional objection to breakfast surviving when heroism does not.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771577838713_3", anchor: "declared it vein depletion", text: "Anomalous cold consuming heat from veins showing no sign of depletion is not vein depletion. It is corruption bleed. The diagnostic profile is identical to readings from the Glow-Fissure's eastern tributaries — cold that eats warmth, source-veins intact, no geological explanation. Lucatransiius knew. I wrote that they knew. They signed it anyway because the Flipper Accord — renegotiated in secret, as I have noted elsewhere, with volume commitments the Nightshelf could not sustain honestly — required those yields. Shaft eight was sacrificed to a contract. The Profun∴lapsum, which flooded those same deep tunnels a generation later, did not arrive from nowhere. It arrived from shaft eight, and from every shaft where someone signed what the Accord needed signed.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771577838713_4", anchor: "reopening in combat generations later", text: "Generations. A spear wound. Reopening. I let this stand because I promised the Nightshelf sources their due, but I want the reader to perform the arithmetic I declined to perform in the main text. Orca tissue heals. Pressure-depth magic could theoretically sustain a wound across decades — but no source invokes it here, because invoking it would require admitting a dying penguin performed blood-communion with the deep, which is theologically inconvenient for a memorial narrative. So instead: a wound that simply forgot how to close. Marvelous.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
